[32m+[m[32m# Hello World DevOps Lab[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA tiny, familiar web app for learning GitHub and AWS DevOps work. It serves `Hello, world!` at `/` and returns a simple health response from `/health`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWe will use this same app as the workload while learning source control, Linux and networking, EC2, containers, ECR, ECS, deployments, and monitoring. The first version runs locally and listens only on your computer.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What you need[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Python 3.10 or newer[m
[32m+[m[32m- PowerShell[m
[32m+[m[32m- Git[m
[32m+[m[32m- GitHub CLI (`gh`) for the GitHub command exercises[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Run it manually in PowerShell[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen PowerShell in this project folder and check Python:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython --version[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCreate and activate a virtual environment. This keeps the project's Python packages separate from other projects:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m venv .venv[m
[32m+[m[32m.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf PowerShell blocks activation, use the environment's Python directly:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32m.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32m.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe app.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOtherwise, install the dependency and start the app:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m pip install -r requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32mpython app.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKeep that terminal open. The server listens only on your computer at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Try the app from a second PowerShell window[m
[32m+[m
